<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Cahan dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ó Catháin, O'Kane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Cahans, Ó Catháin, were a Gaelic ruling family in the north of present-day County <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derry">Londonderry</a>, Ireland, from the 12th century to the early 17th. As chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the O'Neills they took part in their inauguration at Tullyhogue. Their lands were confiscated after the Flight of the Earls and planted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> companies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ocahan-dynasty.jpg" alt="O'Cahan dynasty" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LiamKeane.com · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_family-sept_ir_OCahan_(Keane).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
